From: xbin <xbin@xbin.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] opt-in FUSE writeback cache + HANDLE_KILLPRIV

Adds two missing opt-ins go-fuse never wired despite carrying the
capability constants:

- MountOptions.EnableWritebackCache (FUSE_WRITEBACK_CACHE): the kernel
  buffers writes in the page cache and flushes them as large aligned
  WRITE requests, and shared writable mmap starts working.
- MountOptions.HandleKillpriv (FUSE_HANDLE_KILLPRIV): the filesystem
  promises to clear suid/sgid/security.capability on write and truncate
  itself, so the kernel skips its pre-write privilege checks — including
  the getxattr("security.capability") it otherwise issues per write.

Used by xbin's patched gocryptfs in -xbin-single-tenant mode
(hack/gocryptfs-patches/), where the daemon is the backing tree's sole
writer. Written against go-fuse v2.8.0.
---
diff -ruN a/fuse/api.go b/fuse/api.go
--- a/fuse/api.go	2026-08-03 23:33:41.036262096 +0200
+++ b/fuse/api.go	2026-08-03 23:33:41.045945567 +0200
@@ -278,6 +278,24 @@
 	// kernel to issue a new Readlink call.
 	EnableSymlinkCaching bool
 
+	// EnableWritebackCache requests the FUSE writeback cache
+	// (FUSE_WRITEBACK_CACHE): the kernel buffers writes in the page cache
+	// and flushes them in large, aligned requests, instead of forwarding
+	// every write() call synchronously. This also makes shared writable
+	// mmap work. Caveats: WRITE requests arrive from kernel writeback
+	// (batched, possibly out of order, with kernel — not caller —
+	// context), and the kernel maintains size/mtime/ctime between
+	// flushes, so the daemon's attributes for dirty files lag. Only safe
+	// when nothing modifies the backing files behind the mount's back.
+	EnableWritebackCache bool
+
+	// HandleKillpriv promises that the filesystem itself clears
+	// suid/sgid/security.capability on write and truncate
+	// (FUSE_HANDLE_KILLPRIV). The kernel then skips its own pre-write
+	// privilege checks — including the getxattr("security.capability")
+	// it otherwise issues before every write.
+	HandleKillpriv bool
+
 	// If set, ask kernel not to do automatic data cache invalidation.
 	// The filesystem is fully responsible for invalidating data cache.
 	ExplicitDataCacheControl bool
diff -ruN a/fuse/opcode.go b/fuse/opcode.go
--- a/fuse/opcode.go	2026-08-03 23:33:41.036972831 +0200
+++ b/fuse/opcode.go	2026-08-03 23:33:41.046972939 +0200
@@ -111,6 +111,14 @@
 	if server.opts.EnableAcl {
 		kernelFlags |= CAP_POSIX_ACL
 	}
+	if server.opts.EnableWritebackCache {
+		// Only if the kernel offers it (v3.15+).
+		kernelFlags |= input.Flags64() & CAP_WRITEBACK_CACHE
+	}
+	if server.opts.HandleKillpriv {
+		// Only if the kernel offers it (v4.9+).
+		kernelFlags |= input.Flags64() & CAP_HANDLE_KILLPRIV
+	}
 	if server.opts.SyncRead {
 		// Clear CAP_ASYNC_READ
 		kernelFlags &= ^uint64(CAP_ASYNC_READ)
